# Scacelith - Bahasa Indonesia
#
# Translation of assets/i18n/en.lang (same keys, same {n}). Plurals: Indonesian has a single form
# (a noun after a number stays singular: "3 langkah"), so plural values have one form and no '|'.
# Register: formal "Anda" (always capitalised) and imperatives without a pronoun on buttons, as in
# Indonesian software. Chess terms follow the Indonesian glossary (glossary/id.md): menteri, benteng,
# gajah, kuda, remis, skakmat, pat, rokade; piece letters R M B G K. Units: "dtk" (detik) and "mnt"
# (menit) as Indonesian software abbreviates them; ms, MB, m/s and Elo stay as they are.
# Titles are in capitals (the title face is an inscriptional capital face).

